# Cloudflare Pages redirects. First match wins, so the specific project slugs
# must come before the /portfolio/* catch-alls.
#
# Old site: Docusaurus, docs at /portfolio/*, blog at /blog/*, contact page.
# New site: projects at /projects/*, everything else is a home-page section.
#
# Every exact rule is written twice, bare and with a trailing slash. Astro's
# sitemap emits the trailing-slash form as canonical and Pages 308s the bare
# form to it, so the indexed URL is the one carrying the slash — a rule that
# omits it 404s precisely the traffic it exists to catch. Splat rules already
# match both forms and are not duplicated.

# --- Renamed project slugs (EN) ---
/portfolio/projects/famsecurity    /projects/fam-security  301
/portfolio/projects/famsecurity/   /projects/fam-security  301

# --- Renamed project slugs (PT-BR) ---
/pt-br/portfolio/projects/famsecurity    /pt-br/projects/fam-security  301
/pt-br/portfolio/projects/famsecurity/   /pt-br/projects/fam-security  301

# --- Docs pages that became home-page sections ---
/portfolio/experience         /#experience        301
/portfolio/experience/        /#experience        301
/portfolio/education          /#about             301
/portfolio/education/         /#about             301
/portfolio/intro              /                   301
/portfolio/intro/             /                   301
/pt-br/portfolio/experience   /pt-br/#experience  301
/pt-br/portfolio/experience/  /pt-br/#experience  301
/pt-br/portfolio/education    /pt-br/#about       301
/pt-br/portfolio/education/   /pt-br/#about       301
/pt-br/portfolio/intro        /pt-br              301
/pt-br/portfolio/intro/       /pt-br              301

# --- Project index and any remaining docs route ---
/portfolio/projects         /projects        301
/portfolio/projects/        /projects        301
/pt-br/portfolio/projects   /pt-br/projects  301
/pt-br/portfolio/projects/  /pt-br/projects  301
/portfolio/*                /projects        301
/pt-br/portfolio/*          /pt-br/projects  301

